# ============================================================
# Credit Policy Tool v2 — AI Provider Configuration (OPTIONAL)
#
# The app is fully functional WITHOUT any of these set.
# AI features (segment explanations, scenario narration,
# executive summaries in exported reports) gracefully
# fall back to deterministic templates when no provider
# is configured.
#
# Set env vars BEFORE launching the app:
#   On Windows (cmd):    set OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
#   On Windows (ps):     $Env:OPENAI_API_KEY = "sk-..."
#   On macOS / Linux:    export OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# ============================================================

# ---- Option A: OpenAI ----------------------------------------
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini                   # optional, defaults to gpt-4o-mini

# ---- Option B: Azure OpenAI ----------------------------------
# AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY=...
# AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT=https://your-resource.openai.azure.com
# AZURE_OPENAI_DEPLOYMENT=gpt-4o-mini        # your Azure deployment name
# AZURE_OPENAI_API_VERSION=2024-06-01        # optional, has a sane default

# ---- Option C: Anthropic (Claude) ----------------------------
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001  # optional

# ---- Force a specific provider when multiple are set --------
# LLM_PROVIDER=openai   # or "azure" or "anthropic"
